# Server profiles compiled into production builds (npm run build, build:win, CI).
# Public information only: these addresses are visible to anyone using the app. NEVER put secrets,
# LiveKit keys or the DuckDNS token in any RENDERER_VITE_* variable (they ship in the JavaScript).
#
# Format: Label|URL, comma-separated, at most 5. The first one is the default for new installs;
# a saved sign-in always reopens on the server it belongs to. https:// is required for internet
# hosts (the build fails otherwise); http:// only for private network addresses.
# A git-ignored .env.production.local can override this for local experiments.
RENDERER_VITE_SERVERS=Discord 2.0 — Internet|https://landhoev3.duckdns.org,Discord 2.0 — Home Network|http://192.168.68.65:3001
